#: src/screens/Searches.jsx:110
msgid "Reads Canadian jobs from employer career sites through the RSS search of eluta.ca: no login and no key. Location is a city with a 50 km radius; empty means all of Canada. Eluta has no remote filter. It allows 10 RSS checks a day from one address, so give each search a run interval of 1440 minutes. One run reads one feed page and at most 6 job pages; the other new jobs wait for the next run."
msgstr ""

#: src/screens/Searches.jsx:108
msgid "Reads the job APIs and feeds of Behance, Hollylist, Wana Create, Dribbble, ArtStation and Work With Indies directly: no login and no Apify key. Remote applies on every board: where a board cannot filter it, the jobs that the posting calls on-site or hybrid are dropped. Location (a city name) applies on Hollylist, Wana Create, Dribbble, ArtStation and Work With Indies (remote jobs stay); Behance ignores it. On Remote searches, Country drops the Behance jobs that are not open to that country. Hollylist members-only offers are skipped, and a salary is stored as a number only in US dollars per year. Test reads at most 20 job pages."
msgstr ""

#: src/screens/Searches.jsx:109
msgid "Reads the public API of himalayas.app: no login and no key. Every job is remote, so there is no Remote or Location. Country keeps the jobs open to that country, worldwide jobs included. A salary is stored as a number only in US dollars per year."
msgstr ""

#: src/screens/Searches.jsx:107
msgid "Reads TrulyRemoteWork.com’s full corpus of worldwide-remote roles. Every listing is remote with no location restriction, so you narrow it with the title and company filters below. Each new job’s description is read from its own page; Test reads at most 20 of those pages."
msgstr ""

